# Hy4's other terms (engram lookups, the sparse attention's indexer, launch latency) take it to 20..40 [derived, not measured].
kind: baseline
question: what decode rate does Hy4-flash Q4_K_M serve at depth 512 on the DGX Spark at the serving defaults?
term: tg tok/s @ n=128, depth 512, bloomery-serve at the serving defaults (no --ctx-size), GB10 128 GB unified
unit: tok/s
predict: 20..40
condition: the Spark with no foreign compute process, the SPARK-4Bit download paused, the page cache dropped first; tools/release/sitting.sh --binary portable on the sm121a tarball, two rounds, cells-0.3.15-spark-hy4.tsv
reason: the bytes a token reads at Q4_K_M over GB10's memory bandwidth, the plan's all-on-card placement.
decide-in: the README's GB10 table takes the measured means with their rounds
